  "rules": [
    {
      "uid": "bd3c6e30-167b-4522-afd3-0c357df60f58",
      "alias": "r1",
      "statement": "Synthetic ticker policy: (1) For an organization name with multiple significant tokens, form the base symbol by concatenating the uppercase first character of each significant token, preserving digits when they are significant tokens or token-leading characters. (2) Before forming a base symbol, omit leading articles, legal entity designators, and the conjunction or separator “&”; treat hyphens and apostrophes as internal punctuation rather than as sources of additional initials, and normalize accented letters to their unaccented equivalents. (3) For a single significant-token organization name, use the first four uppercase letters of that token as the base symbol. (4) When an organization name ends with “Class X,” append “.X” to the base symbol, using the class letter in uppercase; do not otherwise change the base-symbol construction."
    }
  ],
